<title>NETHERLANDS: DUTCH CENTRAL BANK ALLOCATES FRESH LIQUIDITY.</title>
<headline>DUTCH CENTRAL BANK ALLOCATES FRESH LIQUIDITY.</headline>
<dateline>AMSTERDAM 1996-12-30</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Dutch central bank said it allocated 7.74 billion guilders to the money market under a one-day special advances pact at an unchanged rate of 2.50 percent.</p>
<p>Individual banks' applications were met for 23.5 percent.</p>
<p>The pact replaces a six-day facility of 5.81 billion guilders which expired today.</p>
<p>-- Amsterdam newsdesk +31 20 504 5000</p>
</text>
